From ef502a945ccbfe11de7fbeb10226f7b63a6d3922 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 24 Jul 2026 19:14:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Rebuild the body around the brain: real routing, motion, and
 Ask Jeremiah
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The body was still 22 checkpoints of incremental patches on the original
one-standard prototype: hand-rolled sessionStorage routing with no real
URLs, a duplicated-inline-style page per feature, and an elaborate
"entry intent" framing system for little payoff. This replaces it wholesale
while leaving the brain (standardsRegistry.js) and grading mouthpiece
(grade-response) untouched — they were already correct.

Routing: added react-router-dom. Real URLs (/map, /classroom/:standardCode,
/ask, /progress, /profile), working browser back/forward, no more
onNavigate prop-drilling or route strings in sessionStorage. Classroom is
reached by clicking a node on the Doctrine Map rather than a permanent nav
tab, matching how a course map differs from a lesson.

Motion: added framer-motion (shared/motion.js). Real ignite-glow animation
when a standard is mastered on the Map, animated stage transitions in
Classroom, animated chat messages and a thinking indicator in Ask Jeremiah.

Ask Jeremiah: a new first-class chat surface (features/ask), backed by a
new ask-jeremiah Edge Function. Open conversation, but still constrained by
the Brain — the full standards list is sent with every request as the only
source Jeremiah may teach from, with instructions to cite standard codes
and say plainly when a question falls outside current doctrine rather than
freelancing. Shares age-band tone guidance with grade-response via a new
supabase/functions/_shared/ageBandGuidance.ts instead of duplicating it.

Simplification: dropped classroomEntryIntent.js (the resume/review/
adaptation/direct framing system) — real progress/resume behavior now
comes directly from the Map plus per-standard saved stage, which already
existed and is simpler to reason about than five checkpoints of framing
copy.

Home and Progress now read real data (getNextUnmasteredStandard,
standardsProgress) instead of static mock objects. Profile's age-band is
now a real control, not a static label, and flows into both mouthpiece
surfaces (localStorage-backed until real auth exists).

Also fixes a latent eslint config gap: core no-unused-vars doesn't
recognize member-expression JSX components (<motion.div/>) as using their
identifier without eslint-plugin-react's jsx-uses-vars rule — added just
that rule, not the full opinionated ruleset.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
